# Standard exclusions
*.md
.git
.github
.idea
.vscode
Dockerfile
CODE_OF_CONDUCT*
CONTRIBUTING*
LICENSE*
SECURITY*

# Node exclusions
dist
node_modules

# App-specific exclusions
coverage
cypress
migrations
output
test
tests

# NOTE: `e2e` is deliberately NOT excluded.
#
# tsconfig.json references tsconfig.e2e.json, whose include is ["e2e/**/*", "playwright.config.ts"],
# and `npm run deploy` runs `tsc -b` — which builds every referenced project. Excluding e2e while
# keeping playwright.config.ts leaves that config importing './e2e/utils' from a directory that is
# not in the build context, and the image build fails with:
#
#   playwright.config.ts(3,25): error TS2307: Cannot find module './e2e/utils'
#
# Excluding playwright.config.ts as well does not help — tsconfig.e2e.json would then match no
# inputs at all (TS18003). This is a multi-stage build and only /app/dist reaches the final image,
# so carrying the e2e sources through the build stage costs context size and nothing else.
# nr-frep, which this tsconfig layout came from, ships no frontend .dockerignore at all.
